1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,706
Inside one candle, three prices in a row. On all three, buyers outweighed sellers more than three to one.

2
00:00:13,155 --> 00:00:17,674
Later price came back to that exact spot, and bounced from there again.

3
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:22,253
This is called a stacked imbalance. That is today's lesson.

4
00:00:23,253 --> 00:00:28,085
Hello, this is episode fifteen of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:28,534 --> 00:00:34,099
Last time: delta divergence. When price and CVD split.

6
00:00:34,549 --> 00:00:40,505
Today: imbalance and stacked imbalance. Where one side pushed hard.

7
00:00:41,505 --> 00:00:47,696
In a footprint every price has two numbers: sold at the bid, and bought at the ask.

8
00:00:48,146 --> 00:00:54,102
When one side's number is many times bigger than the other's, that is an imbalance.

9
00:00:54,552 --> 00:00:58,758
It means one side was in far more of a hurry at that price.

10
00:00:59,758 --> 00:01:03,624
But the comparison is not straight across, it is diagonal. Why?

11
00:01:04,074 --> 00:01:11,780
At any moment, if the bid is 2652, the ask is one tick higher, at 2653.

12
00:01:12,229 --> 00:01:23,306
So whoever bought at 2653 was up against whoever sold at 2652. That is why the ask is compared with the bid one level below.

13
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:34,179
Example: 150 at the ask on 2653. Below it, only 30 at the bid on 2652.

14
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:39,777
150 divided by 30: five times. That is 500%.

15
00:01:40,226 --> 00:01:49,396
Most traders use 300%, three times, as the threshold. Some use 400%. This is a buy imbalance.

16
00:01:50,396 --> 00:01:53,321
Now check the whole candle, top to bottom.

17
00:01:53,771 --> 00:02:05,422
2654: 2.7 times, no. 2653: 5 times, yes. 2652: 3.6 times, yes.

18
00:02:05,872 --> 00:02:12,951
2651: 3.3 times, yes. 2650: less than one, no.

19
00:02:13,951 --> 00:02:20,220
See? Three prices in a row with a buy imbalance: 2651, 2652, 2653.

20
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:28,220
One or two imbalances show up anywhere. But three or more in a row is called a stacked imbalance.

21
00:02:28,670 --> 00:02:33,920
It is a zone where buyers pushed hard on one price after another.

22
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:41,190
The reverse happens too: sell imbalance. Here the bid is compared with the ask one level above.

23
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:48,719
210 at the bid on 2661, only 30 at the ask above: seven times.

24
00:02:49,168 --> 00:03:00,558
4.2 at 2660, 4.3 at 2659. Three in a row: a stacked sell imbalance from 2659 to 2661.

25
00:03:01,558 --> 00:03:04,641
Beware one trap: small numbers.

26
00:03:05,091 --> 00:03:10,733
Three contracts against one is also 300%. But it means nothing.

27
00:03:11,183 --> 00:03:19,150
So set a minimum volume rule. For example, count it only if the bigger side has at least 50 contracts.

28
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:23,938
Now the real use. What does this zone do later?

29
00:03:24,388 --> 00:03:31,232
Price went up to 2670. Then it fell back into the zone, to 2652.

30
00:03:31,682 --> 00:03:42,523
It held there and climbed to 2668. The buyers who pushed there before were standing there again. The zone became support.

31
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:45,796
But it does not happen every time.

32
00:03:46,245 --> 00:03:55,154
Another day price came into the zone and went right through it, down to 2644. Sell imbalances formed on the way.

33
00:03:55,603 --> 00:04:04,851
The buyers were not there any more. So always keep the stop beyond the zone. If the zone breaks, admit it and get out.

34
00:04:05,851 --> 00:04:12,120
And the same truth again: spot forex and gold have no real bid and ask volume.

35
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:18,291
MT5 footprints estimate from ticks. An imbalance on them is an estimate too.

36
00:04:18,741 --> 00:04:25,089
A real footprint comes from futures: gold futures, index futures or a crypto exchange.

37
00:04:26,089 --> 00:04:27,891
So, today's summary.

38
00:04:28,341 --> 00:04:37,667
Imbalance: a diagonal comparison. Ask against the bid below, bid against the ask above. Three times or more.

39
00:04:38,117 --> 00:04:43,603
Three or more in a row is a stacked imbalance: a zone of strong pressure.

40
00:04:44,053 --> 00:04:51,289
Later it can become support or resistance. Ignore small numbers, and keep the stop beyond the zone.

41
00:04:52,289 --> 00:04:58,898
Next episode: absorption and exhaustion. When the push comes but price does not move.

42
